 sustained the injury during Tennessee's win Saturday at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-16T00:39:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50496356/tennessee-leading-receiver-mike-matthews-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma, boosted by crowd's ire at postponement, beats No. 19 Ole Miss","description":"The Oklahoma crowd let Ole Miss know what they thought of having their game delayed by a day, and the Sooners rode that energy to a 24-17 win over the Rebels.","published":"2026-11-16T00:22:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50495687/sooners-boosted-crowd-ire-postponement-beat-rebels","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football SP+ rankings for all 138 FBS teams","description":"The updated SP+ rankings, plus strength of schedule and résumé SP+, after this weekend's results.","published":"2026-11-15T22:56:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49868647/2026-college-football-sp+-rankings-all-138-fbs-teams","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sizing up college football's best races down the homestretch","description":"From spots in the CFP and SEC title game to the hunt for bowl eligibility, there's still a lot on the line.","published":"2026-11-15T22:17:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491637/connelly-college-football-best-races","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC fines Arkansas $500K for allowing fans to storm field vs. South Carolina","description":"The Southeastern Conference fined Arkansas $500,000 on Sunday for allowing fans to storm the field following a 34-6 victory over No. 17 South Carolina.","published":"2026-11-15T22:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493903/sec-fines-arkansas-500k-allowing-fans-storm-field-vs-south-carolina","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Tait Reynolds has torn meniscus, Christopher Vizzina a concussion","description":"Clemson lost starting QB Tait Reynolds for the rest of the season with a torn meniscus, while backup Christopher Vizzina has a concussion.","published":"2026-11-15T21:09:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493355/reynolds-torn-meniscus-vizzina-concussion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Minnesota fires OC Greg Harbaugh Jr., ending third stint with Gophers","description":"Minnesota fired offensive coordinator Greg Harbaugh Jr. as the Golden Gophers rank 15th in the Big Ten in scoring and 17th in yards per game.","published":"2026-11-15T19:36:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491908/minnesota-fires-oc-greg-harbaugh-jr-ending-3rd-gophers-stint","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079420/treydez-green","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trey%27Dez_Green"},"pick":{"pick":21,"round":1,"team":"DAL","via":"GB","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Trey'Dez Green","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trey%27Dez_Green","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:18Z","intro":"Trey'Dez Green (born February 18, 2006) is an American college football tight end for the LSU Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Green was born in Jackson, Louisiana. He attended East Feliciana High School in Jackson before transferring to Zachary High School in Zachary, Louisiana for his senior year. He played football and basketball in high school. In football, Green had 45 receptions for 864 yards with 11 touchdowns his junior year and 53 receptions for 960 yards with 12 touchdowns his senior year. He committed to play college football and college basketball at Louisiana State University (LSU)."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at LSU in 2023, Green played both tight end and wide receiver. He played in all 13 games with two starts and had 13 receptions for 101 yards with four touchdowns. In basketball, he played in six games as a freshman and averaged 1.8 points and 1.7 rebounds."}]}}